The utility is used to configure or display a interface’s parame‐
ters  and  status.   Every interface can be configured with an IP
address using a private key generated  with  an  optional  listen
port,  and a collection of peers.  Each peer has a public key and
allowed IP addresses, and may optionally have a fixed endpoint IP
address and a preshared secret key.  The following  commands  are
supported:  Show  all  peers.  No secret keys are included in the
output.  Show the peer named By default, no secret keys  are  in‐
cluded in the output.  With also display the secret preshared key
that  the peer was configured to have with the option to Show the
private key that was set with Set  the  private  key  of  to  the
base64‐encoded private key in the file at Set the UDP port number
that  listens  for  incoming  sessions on.  This allows a peer to
start a new session without having a specific endpoint IP address
configured.  Add a peer.  The argument may be passed to  and  The
